<%#
  Brambleforce purchase pages — same deliveries as the old skin (the
  gated APK download URL, the unlock code), wearing the game's own
  face. The code stays a single plain text node: buyers copy it, and
  nothing may split its characters.
  Copy truth (2026-10-31): codeEmailed is tri-state — true only when
  the code email really sent (the fresh post-capture render), false
  when it was attempted and did NOT send, null when this is a later
  page-load showing the buyer's session copy (delivery unknown here,
  so the wording claims neither). No branch may promise an email that
  did not verifiably send.
%>
<% if (productId === 'game') { %>
<h1 class="bf-title" style="font-size:clamp(1.55rem,4.6vw,2.3rem);">Your Brambleforce Download</h1>
<p class="bf-lede">Thanks for your purchase! Payment is complete.</p>

<section class="bf-buy-panel" style="margin-top:1.1rem;">
  <h2 style="margin:0 0 .4rem;">Brambleforce — Full Game (Android APK)</h2>
  <p><a class="btn bf-btn-wide" href="<%= downloadUrl %>">Download Brambleforce APK</a></p>
  <ol class="bf-steps" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <li><strong>Open the APK</strong>Find the downloaded file on your Android phone and open it.</li>
    <li><strong>Allow installs</strong>If your phone asks, allow installs from this source.</li>
    <li><strong>Tap Install</strong>Then open Brambleforce — enjoy zero ads.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted fineprint" style="margin-top:.8rem;">Your download can be re-issued from this page anytime — bookmark it. If a purchase email reached you, it links back here too. Lost this page? <a href="/contact">Contact support</a> with your PayPal receipt and we'll sort you out. Optional extras (modes, skins, the expansion) live in the in-game Supply Store — they check out here and unlock with a code.</p>
</section>
<% } else if (productId === 'game_pc') { %>
<h1 class="bf-title" style="font-size:clamp(1.55rem,4.6vw,2.3rem);">Your Brambleforce Download</h1>
<p class="bf-lede">Thanks for your purchase! Payment is complete.</p>

<section class="bf-buy-panel" style="margin-top:1.1rem;">
  <h2 style="margin:0 0 .4rem;">Brambleforce — Windows Edition (PC)</h2>
  <p><a class="btn bf-btn-wide" href="<%= downloadUrl %>">Download Brambleforce for Windows (ZIP)</a></p>
  <ol class="bf-steps" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <li><strong>Download the ZIP</strong>About 1.2 GB — give it a minute on a slow connection.</li>
    <li><strong>Unzip it</strong>Right-click the file → Extract All, then open the folder.</li>
    <li><strong>Run Brambleforce.exe</strong>No installer. First run only, Windows may say "Windows protected your PC" — the build is new and unsigned: choose "More info" → "Run anyway".</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted fineprint" style="margin-top:.8rem;">Your download can be re-issued from this page anytime — bookmark it. If a purchase email reached you, it links back here too. Your campaign saves right on your computer. Lost this page? <a href="/contact">Contact support</a> with your PayPal receipt and we'll sort you out. Optional extras (modes, skins, the expansion) live in the in-game Supply Store — they check out here and unlock with a code, in this edition too: EXTRAS (B) → REDEEM CODE.</p>
</section>
<% } else if (code) { %>
<h1 class="bf-title" style="font-size:clamp(1.55rem,4.6vw,2.3rem);">Your Unlock Code</h1>
<p class="bf-lede">Thanks for your purchase! Payment is complete<% if (codeEmailed === true) { %> — this code was also emailed to you<% } %>.</p>
<% if (codeEmailed === false) { %>
<p class="bf-mail-warning" role="alert"><strong>We couldn't email this code</strong> — our mail didn't go out, so the code on this page is the only copy there is. Copy it now and keep it somewhere safe: it stays visible on this purchase page while you're in this session, and once the session ends it can't be shown again.</p>
<% } else if (codeEmailed === null) { %>
<p class="muted">Here's your code again — it's still yours and hasn't been redeemed. Copy it and keep it somewhere safe: it's shown only while you're in this session.</p>
<% } %>

<div class="bf-code-panel">
  <p class="bf-kicker" style="margin-bottom:.4rem;"><%= product.name %></p>
  <div class="bf-code" id="bf-code"><%= code %></div>
  <button type="button" class="bf-copy-btn" id="bf-copy">Copy code</button>
</div>

<section aria-label="Redeem your code">
  <h2 class="bf-h2" style="font-size:1.3rem;">Redeem it in the game</h2>
  <ol class="bf-steps">
    <li><strong>Open Brambleforce</strong>On the phone where the game lives.</li>
    <li><strong>Open EXTRAS</strong>The B button on the title screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick REDEEM CODE</strong>Type the code above — the unlock is yours for good.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted fineprint" style="margin-top:.8rem;">Codes are single-use — once redeemed, the unlock lives in your game for good.<% if (codeEmailed === true) { %> Your emailed copy is the one to keep for good.<% } else if (codeEmailed === false) { %> If you lose it, <a href="/contact">contact support</a> with your PayPal receipt and we'll sort you out.<% } else { %> If a code email reached you, that email is a second copy. If you lose the code entirely, <a href="/contact">contact support</a> with your PayPal receipt and we'll sort you out.<% } %></p>
</section>
<script>
(function () {
  var btn = document.getElementById('bf-copy');
  var el = document.getElementById('bf-code');
  if (!btn || !el) return;
  btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
    var done = function () { btn.textContent = 'Copied ✓'; setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = 'Copy code'; }, 2000); };
    if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(el.textContent.trim()).then(done, done);
    } else {
      var r = document.createRange(); r.selectNodeContents(el);
      var s = window.getSelection(); s.removeAllRanges(); s.addRange(r);
      try { document.execCommand('copy'); } catch (e) {}
      done();
    }
  });
})();
</script>
<% } else { %>
<h1 class="bf-title" style="font-size:clamp(1.55rem,4.6vw,2.3rem);">Purchase Complete</h1>
<p class="bf-lede">Thanks for your purchase! Payment is complete.</p>

<section class="bf-buy-panel" style="margin-top:1.1rem;">
  <h2 style="margin:0 0 .4rem;"><%= product.name %></h2>
  <p>Your unlock code was shown once at checkout, right after payment. If our code email reached you, that email is your durable copy — codes are stored hashed, so this page can't show the code again.</p>
  <ol class="bf-steps" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <li><strong>Open Brambleforce</strong>On the phone where the game lives.</li>
    <li><strong>Open EXTRAS</strong>The B button on the title screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick REDEEM CODE</strong>Type the code from your checkout page or your email copy.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted fineprint" style="margin-top:.8rem;">Can't find the email — or it never arrived? Check spam for "Your Brambleforce unlock code" first. If the code isn't saved anywhere, <a href="/contact">contact support</a> with your PayPal receipt and we'll sort you out.</p>
</section>
<% } %>

<p class="muted fineprint" style="margin-top:2rem;"><a href="/brambleforce">← All of Brambleforce</a> · <a href="/watch">Watch the shows</a></p>
